{
  "id": "heringbreuer-reflex",
  "term": "Hering–Breuer reflex",
  "definition": "The Hering–Breuer reflex is a classic feedback reflex in which lung inflation, signaled through the vagus nerve, alters breathing. In this packet, it is described as a response that can change over time through nonassociative learning processes such as habituation and desensitization.",
